# Time-boxed exceptions for the Rasta service image scans (ci.yml job
# "Build and scan images", step "Scan image"). One entry per CVE, each with
# the reason it is not reachable and an expiry date; an expired entry turns
# the scan red again on its own.
#
# CVE-2026-115905 (CRITICAL, 2026-10-29 in CI) — Rust `zip` crate 8.5.1, listed
# in node_modules/@temporalio/core-bridge@1.23.0/Cargo.lock (marketplace-service
# image). Inside sdk-core the crate is used only by `ephemeral_server`, which
# downloads and unpacks a local Temporal dev/test server archive; that path is
# reached only through @temporalio/testing (a devDependency) and never by the
# production worker or client, which connect to the deployed Temporal
# frontend. The fix (zip 9.0.5) ships in @temporalio/core-bridge 1.25.0,
# published 2026-10-27 — younger than the seven-day minimum release age until
# 2026-11-03 18:28 UTC. Expires 2026-11-04: by then bump every @temporalio/*
# package to 1.25.0 (lockfile shows core-bridge 1.25.0) and delete this entry
# and, if it is the last one, this file and the `trivyignores` input.
CVE-2026-115905 exp:2026-11-04
